= Andreas Baader freed!

On the 14th of May, Andreas Baader, who was convicted for setting shopping malls on fire in April 1968, was transfered to the German Central Institute for social questions. There, he was supposed to meet journalist Ulrike Meinhof for a book she was writing. Instead, an armed group of six, including Baader's partner Gudrun Ensslin and Meinhof herself, freed him. An employee of the institute was shot and a guard was wounded. Thankfully, both seem to recover.
